      "id": 42459,
      "name": "Vibe Robotics",
      "slug": "vibe-robotics",
      "former_names": [],
      "small_logo_thumb_url": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/small_logos/20d8a5ce151363c695030b892a2be777baa1d339.png",
      "website": "https://viberobotics.co",
      "all_locations": "San Francisco, CA, USA",
      "long_description": "Vibe Robotics builds robots for the work nobody should have to repeat.\r\n\r\nEvery night in every hotel, the same work happens again and again. Towels go up to rooms. Linens move between floors. Laundry gets folded before the morning shift. It’s hard, physical work, and hotels can’t hire enough people to do it.\r\n\r\nVibe 01 is built for exactly that. It carries, delivers and folds. Two arms, a lift column, and a camera head on a base that drives itself through back-of-house hallways and service elevators. It learns by watching people do the job, then does it on its own. Our prototype already folds a towel fully autonomously in 23.8 seconds, a skill it learned from just a few hundred human demonstrations.\r\n\r\nHotels bring Vibe on for a monthly fee, start with one job, and add more as the robot learns. No big upfront cost, and no new system for the team to manage.\r\n\r\nWe’re Archer, Daniel, Katherine and Pranav. We’re starting in hotels and building toward everywhere people work.",
      "one_liner": "Robotics workforce for hotels",
      "team_size": 4,
